{"1-4":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"shinar-h8152","name":"Shinar","kind":"place","brief":"In Mesopotamia","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"words":[{"base":"H3843","lemma":"לְבֵנָה","tr":"le·ve·nah","gloss":"brick","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H3051","lemma":"יָהַב","tr":"ya·hav","gloss":"to give","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":33},{"base":"H9035","lemma":"נוּ","tr":"nu","gloss":"us","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":272},{"base":"H2564","lemma":"חֵמָר","tr":"che·mar","gloss":"bitumen","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H3835","lemma":"לָבֵן","tr":"la·ven","gloss":"to whiten","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H8152","lemma":"שִׁנְעָר","tr":"shin·ar","gloss":"Shinar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H8316","lemma":"שְׂרֵפָה","tr":"se·re·phah","gloss":"fire","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H0259","lemma":"אֶחָד","tr":"e·chad","gloss":"one","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":970},{"base":"H1237","lemma":"בִּקְעָה","tr":"biq·ah","gloss":"Valley (of Jericho)","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H9038","lemma":"הֶם","tr":"hem","gloss":"them","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1125}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"Where can we go? Our brothers have made our hearts melt, saying: ‘The people are larger and taller than we are; the cities are large, with walls up to the heavens. We even saw the descendants of the Anakim there.’”","from":4},{"book":"JHN","chapter":5,"verse":44,"verseEnd":44,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"How can you believe if you accept glory from one another, yet do not seek the glory that comes from the only God?","from":4},{"book":"ACT","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"And when this sound rang out, a crowd came together in bewilderment, because each one heard them speaking his own language.","from":1},{"book":"ZEP","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"For then I will restore pure lips to the peoples, that all may call upon the name of the LORD and serve Him shoulder to shoulder.","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"He has performed mighty deeds with His arm; He has scattered those who are proud in the thoughts of their hearts.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Now the Valley of Siddim was full of tar pits, and as the kings of Sodom and Gomorrah fled, some men fell into the pits, but the survivors fled to the hill country.","from":3},{"book":"DEU","chapter":9,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Hear, O Israel: Today you are about to cross the Jordan to go in and dispossess nations greater and stronger than you, with large cities fortified to the heavens.","from":4},{"book":"PRO","chapter":10,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"The memory of the righteous is a blessing, but the name of the wicked will rot.","from":4}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"5-9":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"babylon-h0894","name":"Babylon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"words":[{"base":"H8193","lemma":"שָׂפָה","tr":"sa·phah","gloss":"lips","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":176},{"base":"H8033","lemma":"שָׁם","tr":"sham","gloss":"there","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":834},{"base":"H1101","lemma":"בָּלַל","tr":"ba·lal","gloss":"to mix","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"H6327","lemma":"פּוּץ","tr":"puts","gloss":"to scatter","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":67},{"base":"H1129","lemma":"בָּנָה","tr":"ba·nah","gloss":"to build","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":376},{"base":"H3381","lemma":"יָרַד","tr":"ya·rad","gloss":"to go down","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":380},{"base":"H2161","lemma":"זָמַם","tr":"za·mam","gloss":"to plan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H0259","lemma":"אֶחָד","tr":"e·chad","gloss":"one","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":970},{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1090},{"base":"H3051","lemma":"יָהַב","tr":"ya·hav","gloss":"to give","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":33}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"His kingdom began in Babylon, Erech, Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":18,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"I will go down to see if their actions fully justify the outcry that has reached Me. If not, I will find out.”","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":2,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"The One enthroned in heaven laughs; the Lord taunts them.","from":6},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"He has performed mighty deeds with His arm; He has scattered those who are proud in the thoughts of their hearts.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"From these, the maritime peoples separated into their territories, according to their languages, by clans within their nations.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"These are the sons of Ham according to their clans, languages, lands, and nations.","from":9},{"book":"PSA","chapter":33,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The LORD frustrates the plans of the nations; He thwarts the devices of the peoples.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"10-26":{"people":[{"id":"arpachshad-h0775","name":"Arpachshad","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":4,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"shem-h8035","name":"Shem","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Noah","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"shelah-h7974","name":"Shelah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Cainan","count":4,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"eber-h5677g","name":"Eber","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shelah","count":4,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"peleg-h6389","name":"Peleg","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Eber","count":4,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"reu-h7466","name":"Reu","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Peleg","count":4,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"serug-h8286","name":"Serug","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reu","count":4,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"nahor-h5152g","name":"Nahor","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Serug","count":4,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"terah-h8646g","name":"Terah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":3,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"haran-h2039g","name":"Haran","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"nahor-h5152h","name":"Nahor","kind":"person","brief":"Abraham's brother","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":25,"uses":496},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":24,"uses":877},{"base":"H2421","lemma":"חָיָה","tr":"cha·yah","gloss":"to live","lang":"h","inPassage":16,"uses":282},{"base":"H3967","lemma":"מֵאָה","tr":"me·ah","gloss":"hundred","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":581},{"base":"H7970","lemma":"שְׁלֹשִׁים","tr":"she·lo·shim","gloss":"thirty","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":172},{"base":"H5152","lemma":"נָחוֹר","tr":"na·chor","gloss":"Nahor","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":18},{"base":"H0310","lemma":"אַחַר","tr":"a·char","gloss":"after","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":715},{"base":"H7466","lemma":"רְעוּ","tr":"re·u","gloss":"Reu","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":5},{"base":"H8286","lemma":"שְׂרוּג","tr":"se·rug","gloss":"Serug","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":5},{"base":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","tr":"bat","gloss":"daughter","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":588}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":1,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"God blessed them and said to them, “Be fruitful and multiply, and fill the earth and subdue it; rule over the fish of the sea and the birds of the air and every creature that crawls upon the earth.”","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":5,"verse":4,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And after he had become the father of Seth, Adam lived 800 years and had other sons and daughters. So Adam lived a total of 930 years, and then he died. When Seth was 105 years old, he became the father of Enosh. And after he had become the father of Enosh, Seth lived 807 years and had other sons and daughters. So Seth lived a total of 912 years, and then he died.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":5,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And after he had become the father of Seth, Adam lived 800 years and had other sons and daughters.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But as for you, be fruitful and multiply; spread out across the earth and multiply upon it.”","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":21,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And sons were also born to Shem, the older brother of Japheth; Shem was the forefather of all the sons of Eber. The sons of Shem: Elam, Asshur, Arphaxad, Lud, and Aram.","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And sons were also born to Shem, the older brother of Japheth; Shem was the forefather of all the sons of Eber.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Two sons were born to Eber: One was named Peleg, because in his days the earth was","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":11,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"This is the account of Terah. Terah became the father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran. And Haran became the father of Lot.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"27-32":{"people":[{"id":"haran-h2039g","name":"Haran","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":4,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"terah-h8646g","name":"Terah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":4,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":3,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"lot-h3876g","name":"Lot","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Haran","count":2,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"nahor-h5152h","name":"Nahor","kind":"person","brief":"Abraham's brother","count":2,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"sarah-h8283","name":"Sarah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Abraham","count":3,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"iscah-h3252","name":"Iscah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Lot","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"milcah-h4435g","name":"Milcah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Lot","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"places":[{"id":"chaldea-h3778","name":"Chaldea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"ur-h0218b","name":"Ur","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"haran-h2771a","name":"Haran","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":31}],"words":[{"base":"H8646","lemma":"תֶּ֫רַח","tr":"te·rach","gloss":"Terah","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":13},{"base":"H2039","lemma":"הָרָן","tr":"ha·ran","gloss":"Haran","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":7},{"base":"H0087","lemma":"אַבְרָם","tr":"av·ram","gloss":"Abram","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":61},{"base":"H8297","lemma":"שָׂרַי","tr":"sa·ray","gloss":"Sarai","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":17},{"base":"H5152","lemma":"נָחוֹר","tr":"na·chor","gloss":"Nahor","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":18},{"base":"H0218","lemma":"אוּר","tr":"ur","gloss":"Ur","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H0802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","tr":"ish·shah","gloss":"woman","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":781},{"base":"H4435","lemma":"מִלְכָּה","tr":"mil·kah","gloss":"Milcah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H2771","lemma":"חָרָן","tr":"cha·ran","gloss":"Haran","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H3876","lemma":"לוֹט","tr":"lot","gloss":"Lot","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":33}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NEH","chapter":9,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"You are the LORD, the God who chose Abram, who brought him out of Ur of the Chaldeans and gave him the name Abraham.","from":31},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"And Stephen declared: “Brothers and fathers, listen to me! The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham while he was still in Mesopotamia, before he lived in Haran,","from":31},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"So Abraham left the land of the Chaldeans and settled in Haran. After his father died, God brought him out of that place and into this land where you are now living.","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So Abram departed, as the Lordhad directed him, and Lot went with him. Abram was seventy-five years old when he left Haran.","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then the servant took ten of his masterʼs camels and departed with all manner of good things from his master in hand. And he set out for Nahorʼs hometown in Aram-naharaim.","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"The Lordalso told him, “I am the Lord, who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldeans to give you this land to possess.”","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then God said to Abraham, “As for Sarai your wife, do not call her Sarai, for her name is to be Sarah.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":22,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Some time later, Abraham was told, “Milcah has also borne sons to your brother Nahor:","from":29}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]}}